==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|sympathetick||obsolete}}
* {{alt|en|sympathetical}}

===Etymology===
Mid 17th century in the sense {{m-g|relating to an affinity or paranormal influence}}, from {{suffix|en|sympathy|etic|t2=pertaining to}}, on the pattern of {{m|en|pathetic}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|efnþrōwiende}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌsɪm.pəˈθɛt.ɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-sympathetic.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛtɪk|s=4}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, related to, feeling, showing, or [[characterize]]d by [[sympathy]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1963|author=w:C. L. R. James|title=w:The Black Jacobins|edition=2nd revised|page=14|passage=Vaublanc, in San Domingo so '''sympathetic''' to the sorrows of labour in France, had to fly from Paris in August, 1792, to escape the wrath of the French workers.}}
#: {{ux|en|John looked very upset. I gave him a '''sympathetic''' look.}}
#: {{ant|en|unsympathetic}}
## Showing [[approval]] of or [[favor]] towards an [[idea]] or [[action]].
##: {{syn|en|approving}}
# {{q|of a person}} [[attract|Attract]]ing the [[liking]] of others.
## {{lb|en|construction}} [[design|Design]]ed in a [[sensitive]] or [[appropriate]] way.
# {{lb|en|relational}} Relating to, producing, or denoting an [[effect]] which arises through an [[affinity]], [[interdependence]], or [[mutual]] association.
#: {{ux|en|'''Sympathetic''' magic is based on imitation or correspondence.}}
#: {{ux|en|[[sympathetic ink|'''sympathetic''' ink]]}}
## {{q|of [[magic]]}} A [[supernatural]] [[connection]] or [[power]] resulting from two items having the same [[form]] or some other [[correspondence]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1936|author=Rollo Ahmed|title=The Black Art|location=London|publisher=Long|page=225|passage=One of his great enthusiasms was for a "'''sympathetic'''" weapon salve, an idea originating in Paracelsus.}}
## {{lb|en|sound}} Relating to [[musical]] [[tone]]s produced by [[sympathetic vibration]] or to [[string]]s so [[tune]]d as to sound by sympathetic vibration.
# {{lb|en|neuroanatomy|neurology|relational}} Relating to or denoting the part of the [[autonomic nervous system]] consisting of [[nerve]]s arising from [[ganglion|ganglia]] near the middle part of the [[spinal cord]], supplying the [[internal organ]]s, [[blood vessel]]s, and [[gland]]s, and balancing the action of the [[parasympathetic]] nerves.
#: {{ant|en|parasympathetic}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Sympathetic''' innervation involves epinephrine.}}

